      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Circuit quantum electrodynamics established a controllable regime for strong light–matter interaction and became a foundational architecture for superconducting quantum information experiments.",
        "attribution": "The theoretical framework and experiments demonstrating strong coupling and coherent control were mutually reinforcing contributions by the named researchers.",
        "maturity": "The central phenomena have been reproduced widely and underpin a mature experimental field, even as scalable fault-tolerant computing remains unfinished.",
