        "Immanuel Bloch",
        "Markus Greiner",
        "Peter Zoller"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Optical-lattice quantum simulation made strongly correlated many-body systems experimentally controllable, opening a distinctive route to studying condensed-matter physics.",
        "attribution": "Zoller's conceptual and theoretical work and the experimental advances by Bloch and Greiner collectively established this program.",
        "maturity": "The methods and core phenomena have been reproduced and substantially extended, though the reach of simulations as reliable solutions to hard material problems remains a live question.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The broad label covers a sequence of advances whose individual credit and scientific limits should be distinguished."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
