        "Carlton M. Caves",
        "H. Jeff Kimble",
        "Roman Schnabel"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Squeezed light converts quantum optics into a practical means of improving interferometric measurements beyond the standard quantum limit.",
        "attribution": "Caves articulated the theoretical measurement principles, Kimble advanced foundational optical experiments, and Schnabel contributed to mature implementations in precision interferometry.",
        "maturity": "The technique has been demonstrated repeatedly and integrated into gravitational-wave detectors, providing strong evidence of durable scientific and measurement value.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The discovery and implementation span several generations of work, so the specific contributions represented here require careful attribution."
        ]
      }
    },
