        "Pablo Jarillo-Herrero",
        "Rafi Bistritzer"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "The prediction and discovery of correlated phases in magic-angle twisted bilayer graphene revealed a new, tunable setting for strong electronic correlations.",
        "attribution": "Bistritzer and MacDonald identified the moiré-band mechanism; Jarillo-Herrero's group demonstrated the striking correlated behavior experimentally.",
        "maturity": "The phenomenon has prompted broad experimental and theoretical study, but the interpretation of particular phases and the generality of the proposed mechanism continue to develop.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The field is comparatively young, and some central questions about superconductivity and competing phases remain unsettled."
        ]
      }
    },
